{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0075526","isObsolete":false,"name":"cap snatching","definition":{"text":"A transcription initiation process during which a nucleotide sequence between 10 and 20 nucleotides in size is cleaved from the 5' end of host mRNAs by a viral RNA-dependent polymerase. The capped leader sequence obtained is subsequently used to prime transcription on the viral genome, which ultimately leads to the synthesis of capped, translatable viral mRNAs.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"839"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"cap snatching involved in viral mRNA transcription","type":"exact"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-30","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0039697 (negative stranded viral RNA transcription)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-30","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0019083 (viral transcription)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-30","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A transcription initiation process during which a nucleotide sequence between 10 and 20 nucleotides in size is cleaved from the 5' end of host mRNAs by a viral RNA-dependent polymerase. The capped leader sequence obtained is subsequently used to prime transcription on the viral genome, which ultimately leads to the synthesis of capped, translatable viral mRNAs."},{"timestamp":"2013-11-30","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A translation initiation process during which a nucleotide sequence between 10 and 20 nucleotides in size is cleaved from the 5' end of host mRNAs by a viral RNA-dependent polymerase. The capped leader sequence obtained is subsequently used to prime transcription on the viral genome, which ultimately leads to the synthesis of capped, translatable viral mRNAs."},{"timestamp":"2013-07-13","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A translation initiation process during which a nucleotide sequence between 10 